    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "<ico-book></ico-book> PRESENT PERFECT vs. PAST SIMPLE",
      "intro": "Una sola pregunta lo decide: <b>¿hay una palabra de tiempo terminado?</b> Si la hay → past simple. Si no la hay → present perfect.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "cells",
          "cells": [
            {
              "h": "PRESENT PERFECT · el resultado ahora",
              "body": "<code>have / has</code> + participio<br>\"We <b>have finished</b> the design.\"<br><span class=\"es\">Importa el resultado, no el cuándo.</span>"
            },
            {
              "h": "PAST SIMPLE · un momento cerrado",
              "body": "verbo + <code>-ed</code> (o irregular)<br>\"We <b>finished</b> it on Friday.\"<br><span class=\"es\">Hay una fecha, y esa fecha ya pasó.</span>"
            },
            {
              "h": "Palabras señal · perfect",
              "body": "already · just · yet · so far · ever / never · this week · since 2020 · for two years"
            },
            {
              "h": "Palabras señal · simple",
              "body": "yesterday · last month · in March · two weeks ago · when I started"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "gold": true,
          "body": "<b><ico-warn></ico-warn> Ojo:</b> <span class=\"x\">\"We have finished it yesterday.\"</span> → <b>\"We finished it yesterday.\"</b> Si dices <i>yesterday</i>, el perfecto se cae. Y al revés: <span class=\"x\">\"I work here since 2021\"</span> → <b>\"I have worked here since 2021.\"</b>"
        },
        {
          "type": "stretch",
          "h": "B2 STRETCH · present perfect continuous",
          "body": "Para la <b>actividad</b> en vez del resultado: \"We've <b>been testing</b> the app for three weeks.\" · \"The team has <b>been working</b> late since May.\"<br><i>We've tested it</i> = hecho, resultado. <i>We've been testing it</i> = en curso, esfuerzo."
        },
